 61NI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2020Ka22:                          
 61NI2c  Phys Rev Lett 124, 132502 (2020)                                       
 61NI c  Compiled by: B. Singh (McMaster), May 18, 2020                         
 61NI c  2020Ka22: E(p)=1.4 GeV beam from the PS-Booster synchrotron at         
 61NI2c  ISOLDE-CERN. The Ni isotopes were produced                             
 61NI3c  in proton irradiation of UC{-x} target by fragmentation, spallation,   
 61NI4c  and fission mechanisms. Nickel atoms were ionized using RILIS (resonant
 61NI5c  laser ionization source), followed by 30-40 keV acceleration and       
 61NI6c  separated using high-resolution mass separator, and transportation to  
 61NI7c  the ISCOOL (radio frequency quadrupole cooler and buncher) apparatus.  
 61NI8c  Measured optical hyperfine structure spectra using collinear laser     
 61NI9c  spectroscopy (COLLAPS) technique on the atomic transitions from        
 61NIAc  3d{+9}4s{+3}D{-3} to 3d{+9}4p{+3}P{-2}, from which change in           
 61NIBc  mean-square nuclear charge radius and isotope shifts were deduced.     
